[{:db/id "q-93815/selection/ebbceb9b1788baae51e40207ba1a3d48c0bae382649ca4fe16d44da7eaa857f1" :answer/id #uuid "5001bc9d-a531-5c6d-9cd8-0e758eeef84f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93815/selection/a72a1a1732d5fbf6285f455439c7d05ab6eb199101d371e3d6253fa78d1923c3" :answer/id #uuid "a5de9abb-f99a-5c53-a7cb-3ce5f3025548" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93815/selection/dd304ebc63bc75ec83eee652e69ddd3dccc0ef9ae7c80993602243cab674970e" :answer/id #uuid "6b977257-2630-5681-8048-c3976e5c0a30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}x+{c}_{2}4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93815/selection/1d580f0e8efb529c9e06af1ec1922a1cbfeafeeb14acac21b436628f470ecb8c" :answer/id #uuid "47ab5f00-efc7-5e63-bc84-a03a5cd26c1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93815/selection/a26d0c0c26b00d336af207a3540fb12b65a97f33d1c397b83ddbc4ec98fe6e98" :answer/id #uuid "8ea510eb-fa4f-5fd3-8dfd-a822ee56bc8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}4{x}^{2}+\\frac{{c}_{2}}{4{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93815/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0cdeed6-8b1f-5283-9603-b832bb5828e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93815/selection/1d580f0e8efb529c9e06af1ec1922a1cbfeafeeb14acac21b436628f470ecb8c" :answer-field/choices ["q-93815/selection/ebbceb9b1788baae51e40207ba1a3d48c0bae382649ca4fe16d44da7eaa857f1" "q-93815/selection/a72a1a1732d5fbf6285f455439c7d05ab6eb199101d371e3d6253fa78d1923c3" "q-93815/selection/dd304ebc63bc75ec83eee652e69ddd3dccc0ef9ae7c80993602243cab674970e" "q-93815/selection/1d580f0e8efb529c9e06af1ec1922a1cbfeafeeb14acac21b436628f470ecb8c" "q-93815/selection/a26d0c0c26b00d336af207a3540fb12b65a97f33d1c397b83ddbc4ec98fe6e98"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93815" :question/id #uuid "35c93618-3c33-5101-a94f-32175a40d7a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-93815" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+16y=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+16{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+16{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +16] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{\\text{4i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{\\text{4i}}}={e}^{\\text{4i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x), \\\\ {x}^{-\\text{4i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{-\\text{4i}}}={e}^{-\\text{4i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =A{x}^{\\text{4i}}+B{x}^{-\\text{4i}} \\\\ y(x) & =A(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))+B(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\ y(x) & =(A+B)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}(A-B)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite $y(x)$ as\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x),\n$$\n\nwhere  ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93815/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbd8ae67-a4f5-5506-9254-9d2ed28b37ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93815"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64788"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +1] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =\\pm \\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{\\text{i}}}={e}^{\\text{i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x), \\\\ {x}^{-\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{-\\text{i}}}={e}^{-\\text{i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =A{x}^{\\text{i}}+B{x}^{-\\text{i}} \\\\ y(x) & =A(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))+B(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\ y(x) & =(A+B)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}(A-B)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite $y(x)$ as\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x),\n$$\n\nwhere  ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-93816/selection/73e42a1890f7d75b6c6ade2049c1467caf65933cc7bd23dedf1bbbe0eeda510f" :answer/id #uuid "7ffdffc2-7878-553a-aaaf-0067639a8464" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{7}+{c}_{2}{t}^{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93816/selection/0937524e5a0cf2a42b3a3e626427bc48df97b1c48bc77f8115fc2257a01456c7" :answer/id #uuid "b7610537-ecc2-52f8-a714-b8193e6d7151" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93816/selection/c7046a6d112566ae68dd3ae9d42a0f71fa09928321a54017b355141f2b8c5355" :answer/id #uuid "7673766e-9ee5-59f9-befc-827443945cf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+7))+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+7))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93816/selection/f4bb2224e4ceb72e4fb927cc1df18251c612394dc0a5d2b1d2b34f11ce6a08ae" :answer/id #uuid "2a2d2bfa-ebda-55bf-b1a3-4b8a18ee447c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93816/selection/d6f7404147c51f11047dabb298b99742cdbe1cf4ebe58d61df6705cdd7c6fe57" :answer/id #uuid "2576d5ac-d3a9-529d-a964-861fab85b1f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93816/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9dd7f711-4cdd-54fe-ba71-283e0a8b9095" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93816/selection/f4bb2224e4ceb72e4fb927cc1df18251c612394dc0a5d2b1d2b34f11ce6a08ae" :answer-field/choices ["q-93816/selection/73e42a1890f7d75b6c6ade2049c1467caf65933cc7bd23dedf1bbbe0eeda510f" "q-93816/selection/0937524e5a0cf2a42b3a3e626427bc48df97b1c48bc77f8115fc2257a01456c7" "q-93816/selection/c7046a6d112566ae68dd3ae9d42a0f71fa09928321a54017b355141f2b8c5355" "q-93816/selection/f4bb2224e4ceb72e4fb927cc1df18251c612394dc0a5d2b1d2b34f11ce6a08ae" "q-93816/selection/d6f7404147c51f11047dabb298b99742cdbe1cf4ebe58d61df6705cdd7c6fe57"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93816" :question/id #uuid "b2b464c8-5a7f-53c2-91f7-e851420cd6e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-93816" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+t{y}^{′}+7y=0,\\,t>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}+t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+7{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }+\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+7{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +7] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +7 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+7 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =\\pm \\sqrt{7}\\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{\\sqrt{7}\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{t}^{\\sqrt{7}\\text{i}}}={e}^{\\text{i}\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ {t}^{-\\sqrt{7}\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{t}^{-\\sqrt{7}\\text{i}}}={e}^{-\\text{i}\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =A{t}^{\\sqrt{7}\\text{i}}+B{t}^{-\\sqrt{7}\\text{i}} \\\\ y(t) & =A(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))+B(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)) \\\\ y(t) & =(A+B)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}(A-B)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite $y(t)$ as\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\n$$\n\nwhere  ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93816/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbd8ae67-a4f5-5506-9254-9d2ed28b37ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93816"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93818/selection/76c1d7521273f5ac67ce47564778e2235a5b20c97d9fcd47f2f3f31e04681937" :answer/id #uuid "0b579818-1e0a-5024-92a9-4d8907b43120" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93818/selection/f6e93db4b107d75aa307864699e89dc381494dfc31f87f1122af8ab6db7a095f" :answer/id #uuid "60f91960-b3f1-5a53-ba11-89a847a74a02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93818/selection/3d5d93579adaf86aeafca5ed6746b4367b91f044d3e7127784ef0e0da4df0cc3" :answer/id #uuid "8b5afbdb-eb2c-5ec8-8178-c608a07269db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93818/selection/8703d14d75d5e2ed91b5626e43c9dd6ad76b52804833c4c761a4cbdbbcdfd017" :answer/id #uuid "ed35335e-0425-5918-9209-236ff48c1bbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93818/selection/e13065333366ccf793b97446ec66f851c59c84deb1c2ba0fdbc49405ebc46886" :answer/id #uuid "3bfb8e52-3f92-541c-86c4-50525f98f9a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+6))+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+6))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93818/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf19b6e8-2156-5439-bed7-bbb77a824352" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93818/selection/8703d14d75d5e2ed91b5626e43c9dd6ad76b52804833c4c761a4cbdbbcdfd017" :answer-field/choices ["q-93818/selection/76c1d7521273f5ac67ce47564778e2235a5b20c97d9fcd47f2f3f31e04681937" "q-93818/selection/f6e93db4b107d75aa307864699e89dc381494dfc31f87f1122af8ab6db7a095f" "q-93818/selection/3d5d93579adaf86aeafca5ed6746b4367b91f044d3e7127784ef0e0da4df0cc3" "q-93818/selection/8703d14d75d5e2ed91b5626e43c9dd6ad76b52804833c4c761a4cbdbbcdfd017" "q-93818/selection/e13065333366ccf793b97446ec66f851c59c84deb1c2ba0fdbc49405ebc46886"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93818" :question/id #uuid "1050ed99-f8d7-582f-ae0b-7e2a882b4a63" :question/math-academy-id "q-93818" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n3{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+3t{y}^{′}+18y=0,\\,t>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}+3t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+18{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 3\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }+3\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+18{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[3\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+3\\lambda +18] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+3\\lambda +18 & =0 \\\\ 3{\\lambda }^{2}+18 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =\\pm \\sqrt{6}\\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{\\sqrt{6}\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{t}^{\\sqrt{6}\\text{i}}}={e}^{\\text{i}\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ {t}^{-\\sqrt{6}\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{t}^{-\\sqrt{6}\\text{i}}}={e}^{-\\text{i}\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =A{t}^{\\sqrt{6}\\text{i}}+B{t}^{-\\sqrt{6}\\text{i}} \\\\ y(t) & =A(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))+B(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)) \\\\ y(t) & =(A+B)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}(A-B)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite $y(t)$ as\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\n$$\n\nwhere  ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93818/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbd8ae67-a4f5-5506-9254-9d2ed28b37ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93818"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64845/selection/8e45e22c2921e7f6b7bfedf72ca8cc72c956731aedac26e9a5d07508a4bbbdbe" :answer/id #uuid "77f087ee-ac22-526b-b875-17b148133a43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64845/selection/f6e93db4b107d75aa307864699e89dc381494dfc31f87f1122af8ab6db7a095f" :answer/id #uuid "46cafe85-15b0-509e-b142-b1b9db85b2d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64845/selection/3bd1edc0cebba454f9b178852e24937abe6a7fa3f71252dd9879e35ab81641e5" :answer/id #uuid "c8934159-7b97-51e7-bbd3-d1670fd6064f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64845/selection/246165fbcca0ef7477cca47f08b36f1b8dc61e970d0b265de853d266d827825b" :answer/id #uuid "e539bedd-d947-5e57-a1c6-c76e3c820551" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{3}+{c}_{2}{t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64845/selection/6c28725a963a86edb1347f385372b2604d67030547e9eed05abe3797a0c056c7" :answer/id #uuid "951a1bbc-8f86-57e1-9331-968cd907dd61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+9))+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+9))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64845/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a85d40e1-9912-5fdb-9e8b-8f47172dc0dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64845/selection/f6e93db4b107d75aa307864699e89dc381494dfc31f87f1122af8ab6db7a095f" :answer-field/choices ["q-64845/selection/8e45e22c2921e7f6b7bfedf72ca8cc72c956731aedac26e9a5d07508a4bbbdbe" "q-64845/selection/f6e93db4b107d75aa307864699e89dc381494dfc31f87f1122af8ab6db7a095f" "q-64845/selection/3bd1edc0cebba454f9b178852e24937abe6a7fa3f71252dd9879e35ab81641e5" "q-64845/selection/246165fbcca0ef7477cca47f08b36f1b8dc61e970d0b265de853d266d827825b" "q-64845/selection/6c28725a963a86edb1347f385372b2604d67030547e9eed05abe3797a0c056c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64845" :question/id #uuid "e2b9b992-e7fe-5e8a-9b74-c0a935c56175" :question/math-academy-id "q-64845" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+t{y}^{′}+9y=0,\\,t>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}+t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+9{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }+\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+9{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +9] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +9 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =\\pm 3\\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{3\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{t}^{3\\text{i}}}={e}^{\\text{i}3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t), \\\\ {t}^{-3\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{t}^{-3\\text{i}}}={e}^{-\\text{i}3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =A{t}^{3\\text{i}}+B{t}^{-3\\text{i}} \\\\ y(t) & =A(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))+B(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)) \\\\ y(t) & =(A+B)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}(A-B)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite $y(t)$ as\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\n$$\n\nwhere  ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64845/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbd8ae67-a4f5-5506-9254-9d2ed28b37ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64845"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64848"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n2{t}^{2}{y}^{″}-2t{y}^{′}+6y=0,\\,t>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}-2t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+6{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 2\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }-2\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+6{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-2\\lambda +6] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-2\\lambda +6 & =0 \\\\ 2{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +6 & =0 \\\\ 2({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +3) & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +3 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve the auxiliary equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +3 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +1)-1+3 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)^{2} & =-2 \\\\ \\lambda -1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =1\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =1\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{1+\\sqrt{2}\\text{i}} & =t{e}^{\\text{i}\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}=t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)), \\\\ {t}^{1-\\sqrt{2}\\text{i}} & =t{e}^{-\\text{i}\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}=t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =A{t}^{1+\\sqrt{2}\\text{i}}+B{t}^{1-\\sqrt{2}\\text{i}} \\\\  & =At(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))+Bt(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)) \\\\  & =(A+B)t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}(A-B)t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite $y(t)$ as \n\n$$\ny(t)=t({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-64847/selection/d1a7f37b737d06f2f6b0bccf9be26c4792f071021570bb52005c6f15136bbe14" :answer/id #uuid "0ec86623-18f4-5786-bd8c-c44a615cb816" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={x}^{3}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64847/selection/a16545fabee8caa3d7fdb4ffaac8675c482d3002a1f6b7f2b2af37e594422c0a" :answer/id #uuid "912e830b-93bd-5a69-abdf-f6732d61d2c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=x({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64847/selection/14832e7ce9b6030fe9568a3c0249a7871e7efffcb15f6f97291d6f7c696873b9" :answer/id #uuid "587fec66-8a6c-5275-937c-c5195b6279a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64847/selection/81266cb1579856eb48760287e5bc7086a47f8f6730a82f92024443c5c65991f9" :answer/id #uuid "c623dc66-c62d-5f28-bff9-b90546697151" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={x}^{2}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64847/selection/8a2f3895015386ef5b4385b8f99f282d2c4471b7ceb7a96cd646d5a1ee5a8571" :answer/id #uuid "46c3244b-859f-58dc-bf34-51a54cc5b46e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+3))+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+3))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64847/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c570e1ff-c95e-59fc-ad8c-6d6d88a2b82e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64847/selection/d1a7f37b737d06f2f6b0bccf9be26c4792f071021570bb52005c6f15136bbe14" :answer-field/choices ["q-64847/selection/d1a7f37b737d06f2f6b0bccf9be26c4792f071021570bb52005c6f15136bbe14" "q-64847/selection/a16545fabee8caa3d7fdb4ffaac8675c482d3002a1f6b7f2b2af37e594422c0a" "q-64847/selection/14832e7ce9b6030fe9568a3c0249a7871e7efffcb15f6f97291d6f7c696873b9" "q-64847/selection/81266cb1579856eb48760287e5bc7086a47f8f6730a82f92024443c5c65991f9" "q-64847/selection/8a2f3895015386ef5b4385b8f99f282d2c4471b7ceb7a96cd646d5a1ee5a8571"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64847" :question/id #uuid "9bcdddf5-359f-511d-bc55-6f46505f28d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-64847" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-5x{y}^{′}+12y=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}-5x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+12{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }-5\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+12{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-5\\lambda +12] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-5\\lambda +12 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +12 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve the auxiliary equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +12 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +9)-9+12 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)^{2} & =-3 \\\\ \\lambda -3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =3\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =3\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}} & ={x}^{3}{e}^{\\text{i}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}={x}^{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\ {x}^{3-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}} & ={x}^{3}{e}^{-\\text{i}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}={x}^{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =A{x}^{3+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}}+B{x}^{3-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}} \\\\  & =A{x}^{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))+B{x}^{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\  & =(A+B){x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}(A-B){x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite $y(x)$ as\n\n$$\ny(x)={x}^{3}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64847/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5937a559-6911-591f-a77c-74ace6d4d659"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64847"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93885/selection/d5e676c5a4e60615781f2de514ef5723e3b7c61a80e542e5e7b54cb63b18923e" :answer/id #uuid "1b718d21-ff8e-54f6-b054-af049ccb4440" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93885/selection/3673c2ba5c4893d8e8e5801163c9e2473e9beaef6c2a9762c3a898204ee75bfb" :answer/id #uuid "16d3bcf2-2f2c-5143-bf52-22aa674b3d0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=x({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93885/selection/5dfaad25f5711aedf53a864c5d8b6928c384761ce0d34f8d87710d3da3bcca11" :answer/id #uuid "cbf8a45d-cbf1-50fc-9899-f14c108aa89e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={c}_{1}{e}^{1+\\sqrt{5}x}+{c}_{2}x{e}^{1-\\sqrt{5}x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93885/selection/42690c6e1f3d11080d3aaf848478492377cb495e9a68cd7fbbefe3590afc940d" :answer/id #uuid "e9656b47-7664-5aa6-a67a-de09b14ee8f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=x({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93885/selection/01c0d9a8da3f45ab33c1612b266d939e70750a2cece7bf0e00b8e2117a94aacc" :answer/id #uuid "251db698-ab56-51fa-a03f-d737e9bad7a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={x}^{2}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93885/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "32e39365-c2ce-579a-89d8-97ffd051ee3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93885/selection/3673c2ba5c4893d8e8e5801163c9e2473e9beaef6c2a9762c3a898204ee75bfb" :answer-field/choices ["q-93885/selection/d5e676c5a4e60615781f2de514ef5723e3b7c61a80e542e5e7b54cb63b18923e" "q-93885/selection/3673c2ba5c4893d8e8e5801163c9e2473e9beaef6c2a9762c3a898204ee75bfb" "q-93885/selection/5dfaad25f5711aedf53a864c5d8b6928c384761ce0d34f8d87710d3da3bcca11" "q-93885/selection/42690c6e1f3d11080d3aaf848478492377cb495e9a68cd7fbbefe3590afc940d" "q-93885/selection/01c0d9a8da3f45ab33c1612b266d939e70750a2cece7bf0e00b8e2117a94aacc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93885" :question/id #uuid "6bb1a549-a5cb-5f20-8612-71cfc9ba2a7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-93885" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+6y=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}-x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+6{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }-\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+6{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-\\lambda +6] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-\\lambda +6 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve the auxiliary equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +1 & =-5 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)^{2} & =-5 \\\\ \\lambda -1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =1\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =1\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{1+\\sqrt{5}\\text{i}} & =x{e}^{\\text{i}\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=x(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)), \\\\ {x}^{1-\\sqrt{5}\\text{i}} & =x{e}^{-\\text{i}\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=x(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =A{x}^{1+\\sqrt{5}\\text{i}}+B{x}^{1-\\sqrt{5}\\text{i}} \\\\  & =Ax(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))+Bx(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\  & =(A+B)x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}(A-B)x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite $y(x)$ as \n\n$$\ny(x)=x({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93885/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5937a559-6911-591f-a77c-74ace6d4d659"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93885"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93886/selection/8559fe1e6d5f3ccbb6118d64270f6117b48d3d776538c7a5ddb9815fb802820b" :answer/id #uuid "f0619ba8-d786-5e0c-9e96-0bc0e0d3