n/8c8306cefe7313c1fcfe68e28c5466b4727c5dc2f5cee27084c2e69272422e41" "q-93886/selection/b994a7db68eadc25879cd888423a3e304a9f80a7a6edf29889174fe2e1f8d40d" "q-93886/selection/f6e93db4b107d75aa307864699e89dc381494dfc31f87f1122af8ab6db7a095f" "q-93886/selection/cbdbeaf9c8cbdc34d70089cddc4546dc951e874e0fee02616a022c9053d935fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93886" :question/id #uuid "1322eb8e-8672-5e3f-ad89-27f6b07b6868" :question/math-academy-id "q-93886" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}-3t{y}^{′}+7y=0,\\,t>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}-3t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+7{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }-3\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+7{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-3\\lambda +7] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-3\\lambda +7 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +7 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve the auxiliary equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4 & =-3 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2} & =-3 \\\\ \\lambda -2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =2\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =2\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}} & ={t}^{2}{e}^{\\text{i}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}={t}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)), \\\\ {t}^{2-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}} & ={t}^{2}{e}^{-\\text{i}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}={t}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =A{t}^{2+\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}}+B{t}^{2-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}} \\\\  & =A{t}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))+B{t}^{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)) \\\\  & =(A+B){t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}(A-B){t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite $y(t)$ as \n\n$$\ny(t)={t}^{2}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93886/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5937a559-6911-591f-a77c-74ace6d4d659"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93886"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64849/selection/f5aa08db63febc35d0c306cc9b02be262c86cd678418a52dfd80dc6fb1978fdc" :answer/id #uuid "e4858f54-35dd-5ae3-81d7-f0714050da8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={t}^{-3}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64849/selection/5893cc8c0f49b501bf434ede6e684a398af33e8e89bd4a5698164ec2d05a12f5" :answer/id #uuid "fc501ed6-7262-5489-b83f-9160db69a30d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={t}^{-3}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6