worked-solution "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}+7t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+13{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }+7\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+13{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+7\\lambda +13] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+7\\lambda +13 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +13 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve the auxiliary equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +13 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +9)-9+13 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ \\lambda +3 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-3\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =-3\\pm 2\\text{i}.$\n\nNote that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{-3+2\\text{i}} & ={t}^{-3}{e}^{\\text{i}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}={t}^{-3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)), \\\\ {t}^{-3-2\\text{i}} & ={t}^{-3}{e}^{-\\text{i}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}={t}^{-3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =A{t}^{-3+2\\text{i}}+B{t}^{-3-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =A{t}^{-3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))+B{t}^{-3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)) \\\\  & =(A+B){t}^{-3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}(A-B){t}^{-3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite $y(t)$ as\n\n$$\ny(t)={t}^{-3}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64849/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5937a559-6911-591f-a77c-74ace6d4d659"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64849"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93898/selection/babeaad4922dedbe515c7ceecd682ca5bb75b2e6fa5ea27f0dfdbd790706d889" :answer/id #uuid "843529fc-663e-5c90-bc64-a82332383a38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93898/selection/ed77a4147a15e27733e470b120f1e615bbd54299d1c3a0a4df8355a75d4eab71" :answer/id #uuid "7a9ae501-78da-58b7-bbd6-d28712cb132b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93898/selection/ce3879390c464f43d9c6463159eb8da389e60299ba73699eadc6c1033dc4ce25" :answer/id #uuid "d6cff2e7-e39f-5880-bc73-26d04dafce46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-2))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93898/selection/a0826eed5255b752819bb691301c1abe78122d16f9015071a08257be986a69cf" :answer/id #uuid "2a9d370f-22fd-5738-b655-3ae51cb31284" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93898/selection/7e156372b5fb1c5dec28f9bd1300dd2c6333f4ac6c793f6f261de5d6659bcbaa" :answer/id #uuid "3a7f0fb7-21bd-5e21-965c-128c46d2c208" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93898/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c5fd4d2-0ccc-5784-95c7-6a96aff804b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93898/selection/7e156372b5fb1c5dec28f9bd1300dd2c6333f4ac6c793f6f261de5d6659bcbaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-93898/selection/babeaad4922dedbe515c7ceecd682ca5bb75b2e6fa5ea27f0dfdbd790706d889" "q-93898/selection/ed77a4147a15e27733e470b120f1e615bbd54299d1c3a0a4df8355a75d4eab71" "q-93898/selection/ce3879390c464f43d9c6463159eb8da389e60299ba73699eadc6c1033dc4ce25" "q-93898/selection/a0826eed5255b752819bb691301c1abe78122d16f9015071a08257be986a69cf" "q-93898/selection/7e156372b5fb1c5dec28f9bd1300dd2c6333f4ac6c793f6f261de5d6659bcbaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93898" :question/id #uuid "804d8607-c39e-561a-b75c-8b9b3de7fbe9" :question/math-academy-id "q-93898" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+t{y}^{′}+2y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+t{y}^{′}+2y=0,\\,y(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=1,\\,t>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(1)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n0={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=1,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\sqrt{2}\\,{t}^{-1}({c}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-{c}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(1)=1$ and ${c}_{1}=0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\sqrt{2}{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93898/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0a76d67-24fe-577b-a395-d6374e76f269"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93898"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93894/selection/def294b04e5834fe40af4f005e9051df2c1c2dbfad7a55c352621387734787cb" :answer/id #uuid "c8861d60-d07b-574e-a01c-1f691dee47c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93894/selection/8bc510778fbad3ef614a19448a9b63f3e89fb27071ee427678ea361191a3f710" :answer/id #uuid "1917a084-2490-5b73-a182-235e05482325" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93894/selection/85d8c7aa1a4b6f3adc50728689649be8967fac433bb2a57ab038bdb4b4d2655c" :answer/id #uuid "cd66bb79-dfbd-55ab-8dc3-c0dbebb9fbe1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93894/selection/9e62a82c9db9b9251ca92c3a6339cbebddca7a75225681136e28c306f56a7df3" :answer/id #uuid "fe210187-8f6c-5400-b5f7-aa9bfc7aa322" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93894/selection/8737cd993ca4d6f66a5b2783e8f77503e6236d96fa811e57468af2bee13bb65d" :answer/id #uuid "6859426a-5fda-5699-b1de-4beb82bd9e2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2x)-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93894/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "31860eb5-4e01-5053-b9d8-066bc02100d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93894/selection/85d8c7aa1a4b6f3adc50728689649be8967fac433bb2a57ab038bdb4b4d2655c" :answer-field/choices ["q-93894/selection/def294b04e5834fe40af4f005e9051df2c1c2dbfad7a55c352621387734787cb" "q-93894/selection/8bc510778fbad3ef614a19448a9b63f3e89fb27071ee427678ea361191a3f710" "q-93894/selection/85d8c7aa1a4b6f3adc50728689649be8967fac433bb2a57ab038bdb4b4d2655c" "q-93894/selection/9e62a82c9db9b9251ca92c3a6339cbebddca7a75225681136e28c306f56a7df3" "q-93894/selection/8737cd993ca4d6f66a5b2783e8f77503e6236d96fa811e57468af2bee13bb65d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93894" :question/id #uuid "3c595bfb-0eb8-5a73-af84-d9df6be73f09" :question/math-academy-id "q-93894" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=0,\\,y(1)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=-5,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(1)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n2={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=-5,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={x}^{-1}({c}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-{c}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(1)=-5$ and ${c}_{1}=2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5 & ={c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93894/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0a76d67-24fe-577b-a395-d6374e76f269"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93894"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64850"] :question/problem "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+2x{y}^{′}+32y=0,\\,y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+2x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+32{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 2\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+2\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+32{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+2\\lambda +32] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+2\\lambda +32 & =0 \\\\ 2{\\lambda }^{2}+32 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}.$  \n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\ny(x)=A{x}^{4\\text{i}}+B{x}^{-4\\text{i}}.\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{4\\text{i}}}={e}^{4\\text{i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\ {x}^{-4\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{-4\\text{i}}}={e}^{-4\\text{i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =A{x}^{4\\text{i}}+B{x}^{-4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =A(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))+B(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have set ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$  \n\nNow let's find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$\n\nSubstituting $y(1)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n1={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=0.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =4{x}^{-1}({c}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-{c}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=0$ and ${c}_{1}=1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =4{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-93895/selection/8e78ffe2f7acd98057d56bed955dab5999423a0dec2927e08078983cde45b5b1" :answer/id #uuid "85b28bdb-3942-53a1-a36b-dd8588044855" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+3)+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93895/selection/4088e880830f048f4da3d24a57778bfc7598b09da661072c6f1f8078e3971044" :answer/id #uuid "f7b105a4-644a-5c95-8d6d-9feb3e88eff1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93895/selection/6c89cefe684b99e99c2f4c832ccc74b2a116a759e78d816dbe2d0fae4416a107" :answer/id #uuid "6373c621-a80b-5fdf-a8f2-91765abc9a4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93895/selection/523f79de54abf9c89e287ff6348dd51467eb6132c1d70e1c7192bca7f2d89869" :answer/id #uuid "2b0a0a26-e2ca-558e-81e6-b0acaab30b5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93895/selection/2c2286bb73637224936240bcceee4c91418d7a016357e12ef2c6eb97203c0c9a" :answer/id #uuid "19340cf9-b270-52dc-b216-db380c2c6295" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93895/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ca3032b-8d57-54c7-9ffc-03b9fe24ffd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93895/selection/2c2286bb73637224936240bcceee4c91418d7a016357e12ef2c6eb97203c0c9a" :answer-field/choices ["q-93895/selection/8e78ffe2f7acd98057d56bed955dab5999423a0dec2927e08078983cde45b5b1" "q-93895/selection/4088e880830f048f4da3d24a57778bfc7598b09da661072c6f1f8078e3971044" "q-93895/selection/6c89cefe684b99e99c2f4c832ccc74b2a116a759e78d816dbe2d0fae4416a107" "q-93895/selection/523f79de54abf9c89e287ff6348dd51467eb6132c1d70e1c7192bca7f2d89869" "q-93895/selection/2c2286bb73637224936240bcceee4c91418d7a016357e12ef2c6eb97203c0c9a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93895" :question/id #uuid "f4866e90-c590-5d22-bd61-9fbc46b65ab6" :question/math-academy-id "q-93895" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+9y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+9y=0,\\,y(1)=3,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=1,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(1)=3$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n3={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=1,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =3{x}^{-1}({c}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-{c}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(1)=1$ and ${c}_{1}=3$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =3{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93895/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0a76d67-24fe-577b-a395-d6374e76f269"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93895"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64851/selection/64a35d6408f9e8fdd3b2a85f690339f6808492aba10d3953a448ec12c14c89b6" :answer/id #uuid "9405949a-9ac7-5ae8-877e-177707af5a1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64851/selection/ab520385811798bc3c0c60ed227ca661205a9cc3e33ca2024a2ecefea83ef5d8" :answer/id #uuid "35203b7b-5433-5f73-a008-3ddda9f2f1be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64851/selection/5d9c2ea86337ef31808d5bbdea7635ab197d3131630d79863f02c18a6d32b7ca" :answer/id #uuid "e2a05c57-926e-5f1a-94ce-dfef94216a48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64851/selection/d46c1cf52b7e71348c828c1618f09df07874f444372b8bd073ad604085163e42" :answer/id #uuid "12020099-4b9f-5ab2-a9ca-ef7e8c71f433" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64851/selection/a03c99ff8e63089c3cffdcb4f49c4418d6f66564eadb2d62b1805c59c8f5e48f" :answer/id #uuid "1628f2ab-4c28-5db0-857e-316e9823a487" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64851/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "940048f6-2b31-5c51-86c9-15b9f0ca0396" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64851/selection/ab520385811798bc3c0c60ed227ca661205a9cc3e33ca2024a2ecefea83ef5d8" :answer-field/choices ["q-64851/selection/64a35d6408f9e8fdd3b2a85f690339f6808492aba10d3953a448ec12c14c89b6" "q-64851/selection/ab520385811798bc3c0c60ed227ca661205a9cc3e33ca2024a2ecefea83ef5d8" "q-64851/selection/5d9c2ea86337ef31808d5bbdea7635ab197d3131630d79863f02c18a6d32b7ca" "q-64851/selection/d46c1cf52b7e71348c828c1618f09df07874f444372b8bd073ad604085163e42" "q-64851/selection/a03c99ff8e63089c3cffdcb4f49c4418d6f66564eadb2d62b1805c59c8f5e48f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64851" :question/id #uuid "b6cf60f1-e2bf-5585-b177-3a5dfb2a3ae3" :question/math-academy-id "q-64851" :question/problem "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+25y=0,\\,y(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=-1,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+25{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+25{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +25] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+\\lambda +25 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =\\pm 5\\text{i}.$  \n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\ny(x)=A{x}^{5\\text{i}}+B{x}^{-5\\text{i}}.\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{5\\text{i}}}={e}^{5\\text{i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x), \\\\ {x}^{-5\\text{i}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{-5\\text{i}}}={e}^{-5\\text{i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =A{x}^{5\\text{i}}+B{x}^{-5\\text{i}} \\\\  & =A(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))+B(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have set ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$  \n\nNow let's find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$\n\nSubstituting $y(1)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n0={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=-1.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =5{x}^{-1}({c}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-{c}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=-1$ and ${c}_{1}=0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =5{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =-\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(x)=-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-64851/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0a76d67-24fe-577b-a395-d6374e76f269"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64851"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64857/selection/475844fb2804d0aaed0cf2684d3500d3a0423b424d26920218c41495fdf973f8" :answer/id #uuid "4189d455-cca0-5855-91c2-96a1447433cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=-{t}^{2}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64857/selection/3413f5429bc61bf497a69b0a3f38636fa2b9579f39fee21984b82663c781bdba" :answer/id #uuid "e8b2c369-3327-56c3-ae9e-d597ccf18279" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={t}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64857/selection/24c8eba1b0010d5367d6bb788d88b82a824b025c8fd823ad7c7385e0dfb230c6" :answer/id #uuid "1ae224b1-3c8c-5461-b9d4-5ff18495c311" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)={t}^{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64857/selection/d66d517f0d155ed21a02685194fbd4a081640378ba921d2b0560271b3f165b6c" :answer/id #uuid "43863823-0fcb-5bde-a69e-82922bf926ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=-5{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64857/selection/a50df4882b7cbc5f06ead90659506f8803a4c530723af009c455076a9b7038d3" :answer/id #uuid "21d86bed-17fc-5ff5-9baf-1c1e0cbc4eb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=-7{t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64857/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc9cde6c-c379-58fc-ac63-d2083f8a3bad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64857/selection/3413f5429bc61bf497a69b0a3f38636fa2b9579f39fee21984b82663c781bdba" :answer-field/choices ["q-64857/selection/475844fb2804d0aaed0cf2684d3500d3a0423b424d26920218c41495fdf973f8" "q-64857/selection/3413f5429bc61bf497a69b0a3f38636fa2b9579f39fee21984b82663c781bdba" "q-64857/selection/24c8eba1b0010d5367d6bb788d88b82a824b025c8fd823ad7c7385e0dfb230c6" "q-64857/selection/d66d517f0d155ed21a02685194fbd4a081640378ba921d2b0560271b3f165b6c" "q-64857/selection/a50df4882b7cbc5f06ead90659506f8803a4c530723af009c455076a9b7038d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64857" :question/id #uuid "e5597e1e-627e-5a60-8b6e-d477892d2e30" :question/math-academy-id "q-64857" :question/problem "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}-7t{y}^{′}+20y=0,\\,y(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=2,\\,t>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}-7t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+20{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }-7\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+20{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-7\\lambda +20] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-7\\lambda +20 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +20 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve the auxiliary equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +20 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +16)-16+20 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ \\lambda -4 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =4\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =4\\pm 2\\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{4+2\\text{i}} & ={t}^{4}{e}^{\\text{i}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}={t}^{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)) \\\\ {t}^{4-2\\text{i}} & ={t}^{4}{e}^{-\\text{i}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}={t}^{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =A{t}^{4+2\\text{i}}+B{t}^{4-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =A{t}^{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))+B{t}^{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)) \\\\  & =(A+B){t}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\text{i}(A-B){t}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite the expression for $y(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\ny(t)={t}^{4}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$  \n\nNow let's find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$\n\nSubstituting $y(1)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n0={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=2.$ First, we substitute ${c}_{1}=0$ and  differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =2{c}_{2}{t}^{3}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =2{c}_{2} \\\\ 1 & ={c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={t}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-64857/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60ce6bcb-cfb8-5261-b036-6df775d04184"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64857"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64808"] :question/problem "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+5y=0,\\,y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=-2,\\,x>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+5x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+5{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+5\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+5{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+5\\lambda +5] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+5\\lambda +5 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +5 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe solve the auxiliary equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4 & =-1 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\lambda +2 & =\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =-2\\pm \\text{i}.$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{-2+\\text{i}} & =\\frac{{e}^{\\text{i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}{{x}^{2}}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{-2-\\text{i}} & =\\frac{{e}^{-\\text{i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}{{x}^{2}}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =A{x}^{-2+\\text{i}}+B{x}^{-2-\\text{i}} \\\\  & =A\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{{x}^{2}}+B\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(A+B)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\text{i}(A-B)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite the expression for $y(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\frac{{c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1}=A+B$ and ${c}_{2}=\\text{i}(A-B).$  \n\nNow let's find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$\n\nSubstituting $y(1)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n1={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=-2.$ First, we substitute ${c}_{1}=1$ and  differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{({c}_{2}-2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-(1+2{c}_{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=-2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & ={c}_{2}-2 \\\\ {c}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-93956/selection/f667800a461ef8133df1f8d9b7d5009b84c53e5bdc187c06dff2e8ba6e942fd3" :answer/id #uuid "62e16aeb-ac0f-518b-96f9-7c665980bf6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=2t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-