"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93956" :question/id #uuid "8d61ab3b-c5fe-55e7-b9b2-81835c9cd524" :question/math-academy-id "q-93956" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n2{t}^{2}{y}^{″}-2t{y}^{′}+20y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=t({c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n2{t}^{2}{y}^{″}-2t{y}^{′}+20y=0,\\,y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=-2,\\,t>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(1)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n1={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=-2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =({c}_{1}+3{c}_{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+({c}_{2}-3{c}_{1})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(1)=-2$ and ${c}_{1}=1$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =1+3{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)=t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-93956/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60ce6bcb-cfb8-5261-b036-6df775d04184"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93956"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93951/selection/a190374322c532bf61fbb76e0872451ed72c22213c5ec1c7b11a4c7c87eaf7af" :answer/id #uuid "dd849fe7-3943-5b53-8a82-34dabbd22da8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(t)=t(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93951/selection/00543e5926c3dec3716489492067bd018eef486e1ab2c0696f34024b6a52e1f8" :answer/id #uuid "d3